From b72f3acd5df57148eaf8067dbc928dc5779fafd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:21:51 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Work with hundreds of bodies

Measured on a block patterned to 400 bodies with more features on it. The
results are identical (body IDs, volumes, centres, element maps); only the
time changed: a recompute with nothing changed went from 4.6 s to 0.04 s,
a fillet on 20 of the bodies from 24 s to 1.6 s, a Through All hole at 20
points from 48 s to 1.8 s, rebuilding 10 features from 55 s to 6.5 s.

- Copies (patterns, Move/Copy) share the seed body's topology.
- Volumes, centres and boxes are kept per shape (a copy's from its seed).
- Box tests before booleans and element searches: cuts, holes, Up To
  Next, fillet/chamfer/draft/thread picks, sweep paths, sketch contours.
- References: an index per feature shape finds the body of an element and
  where a mapped name went, instead of walking every element.
- Part sync: one document scan, O(bodies) work, folders re-claimed only
  when their bodies change.
- Panels: only the bodies a preview changes are veiled and redrawn (a
  pattern's copies looked changed), their mesh is kept between previews,
  ghosting writes only what changes, body lists are named once.
- Kept shapes are let go when a document closes.
- Plane labels on the command line follow the planes when FreeCAD resizes
  them (an intermittent test failure).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JLfqHcRTb2RXQ8Vv8Bdrcu
